-- CK-20: a rigid variable inside a derived shape is a sub-wanted on that
-- rigid, and with no `where` clause for it the comparison is
-- `missing_where_constraint` at the `==` (static-dispatch-spike.md §6.2 Rule
-- U2, §6.3; checker-v2.md §9.3's last paragraph). On 7427828 both check
-- clean: the part is answered `err` with no diagnostic, `Lower` answers the
-- hole with structural `Basics.eq`, and the built program compares
-- functions and ignores a custom `eq` (`False False False`).


pairEq : a, a -> Bool
pairEq x y =
    ( x, 1 ) == ( y, 1 )


recEq : a, a -> Bool
recEq x y =
    { v = x } == { v = y }
